---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LEGAL } from '../../data/site-config';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title="IMU Calculator Privacy in Italy: Data, No Cookies, Stability" description="IMU calculator privacy in Italy: inputs stay in your browser, no cookies and no personal data recorded; cookie-free Microsoft Clarity only checks the site is stable." lang={lang} noindex={true} jsonLd={[breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: route('home', lang) }, { name: 'Privacy', path: route('privacy', lang) }])]} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy' }]}>
  <header class="mb-6"><h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-navy-900 md:text-4xl">Privacy policy</h1></header>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <p>This notice, given under articles 13 and 14 of the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR, EU Regulation 2016/679), explains what data is processed when you look up IMU rates or use the calculators on this site.</p>

    <h2>Controller</h2>
    <LegalIdentity lang="en" />
    <p>For privacy questions, write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. No data protection officer has been appointed, as the scale of processing does not require one.</p>

    <h2>The calculators do not send your figures</h2>
    <p>The IMU calculation runs entirely in your browser. The comune, cadastral income, category, ownership share and rate you enter are not sent to us or anyone else, are not stored on a server and are not linked to you. There is no account, no newsletter and no form collecting personal data.</p>
    <p>When you change a field, the calculator writes the values into the page address so you can share the calculation. That address update is not passed to anyone. If you open a link that already contains values, such as one someone sent you, those values are part of the address of the page you visit.</p>

    <h2>Hosting logs</h2>
    <p>The site is hosted by {LEGAL.hosting.name}. Like any web server, the host records the IP address, page requested, date and browser type of each request to deliver the site and protect it from abuse. Legal basis: legitimate interest in running the site securely (GDPR art. 6(1)(f)). We have no access to these logs and do not use them to identify visitors.</p>

    <h2>Anonymous stability check with Microsoft Clarity, without cookies</h2>
    <p>The publisher records no personal data about people who look up IMU rates. To check that pages and the calculator work, we use Microsoft Clarity, a service of Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited (One Microsoft Place, South County Business Park, Leopardstown, Dublin 18, Ireland), in cookie-free mode: before Clarity loads, the site tells it not to use cookies, and Clarity sets none. For each page view it records errors, load times, clicks that lead nowhere and scrolling, without linking visits together; page text and typed values are masked. Microsoft receives the technical data of the request, including the IP address from which it derives an approximate location, and keeps recordings for 30 days and aggregated data for up to 13 months.</p>
    <h3>Legal basis and how to object</h3>
    <p>Legal basis: legitimate interest in offering a site that works (GDPR art. 6(1)(f)); no cookie or identifier remains on your device. You can object at any time by blocking the <code>clarity.ms</code> domain or writing to us. The site uses no other measurement or tracking tool. Details on the <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies page</a>.</p>
    <h3>Advertising</h3>
    <p>The site shows no advertising.</p>

    <h2>Recipients and transfers</h2>
    <p>We do not sell or share data. The only recipients are the host, for technical logs, and Microsoft, for the stability check. The Microsoft group is headquartered in the United States: technical data may be transferred there under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework, under which Microsoft Corporation is certified, and standard contractual clauses. See the <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Microsoft privacy statement</a>.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>The GDPR gives you rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction, portability and objection (articles 15 to 21). For any request, write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>; we reply within one month. As we keep no accounts, we usually hold nothing that identifies you, and we will tell you so. You may complain to the Italian data protection authority (Garante per la protezione dei dati personali) or to the authority of the publisher’s country, the {LEGAL.supervisoryAuthority}.</p>
    <p>Last updated: 6 October 2026.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
